# Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so __pycache__/ and *.pyc are invisible in
# `git status` yet fully present in the build context. In the tor context that
# was 544K of the 964K sent to the daemon, and `COPY wordlists /wordlists`
# baked the .pyc files straight into the published image — making that layer's
# cache key depend on whether the developer had run the test suite. Two of the
# .pyc files had no .py source left in the repo at all (follow-fetch,
# wayback-static), so deleted modules were still shipping as bytecode.
#
# tests/test_onionnames.py and tests/test_onionheaven_integration.py put
# app/Resources/docker/tor on sys.path and import from it, so these
# directories regenerate on every test run — an exclude is the only fix, not
# a one-time delete.
#
# Deliberately a targeted exclude list rather than an exclude-all/allowlist:
# the tor Dockerfile COPYs 18 individually named files, and an allowlist that
# misses one fails late with a confusing "file not found" at COPY time.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.DS_Store
